@@ -430,7 +430,7 @@ holding the public key could read and write users (including `role`), stores, or
 The admin pages and the settings screens (products, services, orders, blog, appearance) were querying Supabase from the
 browser and depended on those policies.
 
-**State checked against production on 2026-10-14:** the lockdown is in effect. Every public table has RLS on; `anon` and `authenticated` hold **zero** table grants; neither can execute any SECURITY DEFINER function; only 8 policies remain. The `20261012*` migrations are not in `supabase_migrations` (they were applied some other way), so do not re-run them blindly; the migration files document intent, the database is the truth. Since then: the `bill-servers-every-10-min` cron job reads its bearer token from Vault (`bill_servers_cron_token`) instead of carrying it in the command (2026-10-23). **Still open, and currently broken:** the `bill-servers` function compares the token to its own `CRON_SECRET` and has returned 401 to every run since at least the morning of 2026-10-23 (before and after the Vault move), so hourly server billing is not running. No servers exist yet (`servers` and `server_billing` are empty), so nothing has gone unbilled. Fix: set the function's `CRON_SECRET` to the value in Vault (`select decrypted_secret from vault.decrypted_secrets where name = 'bill_servers_cron_token'`), or generate a new one and set both together. Then confirm a 200 in `net._http_response`. Rotate that token, which means setting a new value as the function's own secret and in Vault at the same time (any run in between gets a 401), and the legacy Supabase-Auth password forms in `apps/web`.
+**State checked against production on 2026-10-14:** the lockdown is in effect. Every public table has RLS on; `anon` and `authenticated` hold **zero** table grants; neither can execute any SECURITY DEFINER function; only 8 policies remain. The `20261012*` migrations are not in `supabase_migrations` (they were applied some other way), so do not re-run them blindly; the migration files document intent, the database is the truth. Since then: the `bill-servers-every-10-min` cron job reads its bearer token from Vault (`bill_servers_cron_token`) instead of carrying it in the command (2026-10-23). **Fixed 2026-10-23:** the `bill-servers` function used to compare the token to its own `CRON_SECRET` edge secret, which no longer matched, so every run since at least that morning returned 401 and hourly billing did not run (no servers exist yet, so nothing went unbilled). The function also accepted `Bearer undefined` once the secret was deleted. Vault is now the only copy: `check_bill_servers_token(text)` (migration `20261023c_bill_servers_token_check.sql`) compares the caller's token to `bill_servers_cron_token` inside Postgres and fails closed, and the function reads the UpCloud key through `get_upcloud_api_key()` (Vault secret `UPCLOUD_API_KEY`). Both are `SECURITY DEFINER`, executable by `service_role` only. The function has no edge secrets of its own for this (deployed as version 6; its source is not in the repo). Verified: a real token gets 200, `Bearer undefined` gets 401. To rotate the cron token, update the one Vault secret; there is no second copy and no 401 window. **Still open:** the UpCloud suspend path is untested because no servers exist; `apps/web/lib/upcloud.ts` still reads `UPCLOUD_API_TOKEN` from the Vercel env, so the key lives in two places until web moves too; and the legacy Supabase-Auth password forms in `apps/web`.
 
 Code done: admin pages and the docs page use the server client; the five settings screens call server actions in
 `apps/storefront/lib/admin/*` (authorized per store, scoped by `store_id`, plan limits and blog gating now enforced; appearance
